Feature: The context graph
  One graph of the team's repositories, generated by Rubato on a timer and read by agents
  through their own companion (ADR 0084, ADR 0086). The Repos tab says how fresh it is
  (features/repos.feature).

  @context-graph.companion-keeps-a-copy
  Scenario: A paired companion keeps a copy of the graph the server built
    Given the server builds the context graph of the repositories on the map
    And a companion paired by a person on the team is connected
    Then the companion holds a copy of each repository's source, the workspace's and the team's
    And each one is known to be the one the server announced

  @context-graph.by-hand-over-stdio
  Scenario: A session started by hand reads the same graph
    Given a companion that holds a copy of the context graph
    When a session its owner started by hand asks through "rubato-companion mcp"
    Then it is offered five read-only tools and no other
    And it reads what the copy holds, with each source's head and age
